IMPORT `cr2-nouns`

-- Canada Pension Plan Regulations (C.R.C., c. 385), Part V -- DETERMINATION BY THE MINISTER, AND PAYMENT OF THE DEATH
-- BENEFIT TO OTHERS THAN THE ESTATE (regulations 63 and 64).
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively. Source: the Regulations text file, lines 628 to 643.
--
-- Regulation 63: how the Minister establishes who is a spouse, common-law partner, child or parent, or who is dead,
-- and what the applicant or beneficiary must furnish. Regulation 64: when a direction under section 71(2) of the Act
-- may send the death benefit to someone other than the estate, to whom, and how much may go to whoever paid for the funeral.
-- The amount test in 64(1) is dated: two thirds of 10 per cent of the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for a death
-- before 1 January 1998, $2,387 for a death from 1 January 1998 to 31 December 2018, and none for a later death
-- (the text gives none; the other two grounds in 64(1) remain).

§ `Part V -- Determination by the Minister, and the death benefit (regulations 63 and 64)`

§§ `Regulation 63 -- determining a relationship or a death`

-- src:629 | 63 (1) To determine whether a person is the spouse, common-law partner, child or parent of an applicant, contributor or other person subject to a division or whether a person is deceased, the Minister must use
-- src:630 | (a) any information or evidence obtained under subsections (2) to (4);
-- src:631 | (b) any information made available to the Minister by the Canada Employment Insurance Commission under subsection 28.2(5) of the Department of Employment and Social Development Act; or
-- src:632 | (c) any other information that the Minister may obtain.
@ref Reg 63(1) (src:629-632)
GIVEN `the question is whether a person is the spouse, common-law partner, child or parent of an applicant, contributor or other person subject to a division, or whether a person is deceased` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 63(1) — the Minister must use the information in paragraphs (a) to (c) to determine the question`
    `the question is whether a person is the spouse, common-law partner, child or parent of an applicant, contributor or other person subject to a division, or whether a person is deceased` MEANS
    `the question is whether a person is the spouse, common-law partner, child or parent of an applicant, contributor or other person subject to a division, or whether a person is deceased`

-- src:633 | (2) The applicant or beneficiary must furnish the Minister with any certificate of marriage, birth, baptism or death, a copy of any such document, or a copy of any act of marriage, birth, baptism or death, as the case may be, that may enable the Minister to make a determination referred to in subsection (1).
@ref Reg 63(2) (src:633)
GIVEN `the document is a certificate of marriage, birth, baptism or death, a copy of one, or a copy of an act of marriage, birth, baptism or death` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document may enable the Minister to make a determination referred to in subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 63(2) — the applicant or beneficiary must furnish the document to the Minister`
    `the document is a certificate of marriage, birth, baptism or death, a copy of one, or a copy of an act of marriage, birth, baptism or death`
    `the document may enable the Minister to make a determination referred to in subsection (1)` MEANS
    `the document is a certificate of marriage, birth, baptism or death, a copy of one, or a copy of an act of marriage, birth, baptism or death`
        AND `the document may enable the Minister to make a determination referred to in subsection (1)`

-- src:634 | (3) If there are reasonable grounds to doubt the validity of the copy of a document referred to in subsection (2), the Minister may require that the original of the document or, if applicable, the copy of the act issued by the competent authority be furnished.
@ref Reg 63(3) (src:634)
GIVEN `there are reasonable grounds to doubt the validity of the copy of a document referred to in subsection (2)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 63(3) — the Minister may require the original of the document or the copy of the act issued by the competent authority`
    `there are reasonable grounds to doubt the validity of the copy of a document referred to in subsection (2)` MEANS
    `there are reasonable grounds to doubt the validity of the copy of a document referred to in subsection (2)`

-- src:635 | (4) For the purposes of subsection (1), if none of the documents referred to in subsection (2) are available or adequate, the applicant or beneficiary must, at the Minister’s request, furnish the Minister with any other information or evidence that is available respecting their relationship with the person referred to in subsection (1).
@ref Reg 63(4) (src:635)
GIVEN `none of the documents referred to in subsection (2) are available or adequate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister has requested other information or evidence respecting the relationship` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 63(4) — the applicant or beneficiary must furnish other information or evidence respecting their relationship`
    `none of the documents referred to in subsection (2) are available or adequate`
    `the Minister has requested other information or evidence respecting the relationship` MEANS
    `none of the documents referred to in subsection (2) are available or adequate`
        AND `the Minister has requested other information or evidence respecting the relationship`

§§ `Regulation 64 -- the death benefit paid to others than the estate`

-- 64(1): the amount limb. Two thirds of 10 per cent of the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for a death before 1 January
-- 1998; $2,387 for a death after 31 December 1997 and before 1 January 2019; no limb for a death on or after 1 January 2019.
-- src:638 | 64 (1) If paragraph 71(2)(a) of the Act applies or the estate of a deceased contributor has not applied for the death benefit within 60 days after the contributor’s death, or if the amount of the death benefit is less than two thirds of 10% of the Year’s Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the year in which the contributor died, in the case of a death that occurred before January 1, 1998, or less than $2,387, in the case of a death that occurred after December 31, 1997 and before January 1, 2019, a direction under subsection 71(2) of the Act may, subject to subsections (2) and (3), be given for payment of the death benefit
@ref Reg 64(1) (src:638)
GIVEN `the date of death of the contributor` IS A DATE
      `the amount of the death benefit` IS A NUMBER
      `the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the year in which the contributor died` IS A NUMBER   -- out of range: section 18 (piece cp1)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 64(1) — the death benefit is less than the amount the regulation names`
    `the date of death of the contributor`
    `the amount of the death benefit`
    `the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the year in which the contributor died` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the date of death of the contributor` LESS THAN (YMD 1998 1 1)
           THEN `the amount of the death benefit` LESS THAN
                ((2 DIVIDED BY 3) TIMES (0.1 TIMES `the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the year in which the contributor died`))
        IF `the date of death of the contributor` LESS THAN (YMD 2019 1 1)
           THEN `the amount of the death benefit` LESS THAN 2387
        OTHERWISE FALSE

@ref Reg 64(1) (src:638)
GIVEN `paragraph 71(2)(a) of the Act applies` IS A BOOLEAN   -- out of range: section 71(2)(a) (piece cp4)
      `the date of death of the contributor` IS A DATE
      `the date the estate applied for the death benefit` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the amount of the death benefit` IS A NUMBER
      `the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the year in which the contributor died` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`reg 64(1) — a direction under subsection 71(2) of the Act may be given for payment of the death benefit to a person other than the estate`
    `paragraph 71(2)(a) of the Act applies`
    `the date of death of the contributor`
    `the date the estate applied for the death benefit`
    `the amount of the death benefit`
    `the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the year in which the contributor died` MEANS
    `paragraph 71(2)(a) of the Act applies`
        OR estateHasNotApplied
        OR `reg 64(1) — the death benefit is less than the amount the regulation names`
              `the date of death of the contributor` `the amount of the death benefit` `the Year's Maximum Pensionable Earnings for the year in which the contributor died`
    WHERE
        estateHasNotApplied MEANS
            CONSIDER `the date the estate applied for the death benefit`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
            WHEN JUST applied THEN applied GREATER THAN (`the date a time limit ends` `the date of death of the contributor` (`a number of days` WITH `number of days` IS 60))

-- src:639 | (a) to the individual or institution who has paid or is responsible for the payment of the deceased contributor’s funeral expenses;
-- src:640 | (b) in the absence of an individual or institution described in paragraph (a), to the survivor of the deceased contributor; or
-- src:641 | (c) in the absence of an individual or institution referred to in paragraph (a) and a survivor referred to in paragraph (b), to the next of kin of the deceased contributor.
@ref Reg 64(1) (src:639-641)
GIVEN `there is an individual or institution who has paid or is responsible for the payment of the deceased contributor's funeral expenses` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is a survivor of the deceased contributor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is next of kin of the deceased contributor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `cr2 Payee of a death benefit other than the estate`
`reg 64(1) — the payee of the death benefit when a direction is given`
    `there is an individual or institution who has paid or is responsible for the payment of the deceased contributor's funeral expenses`
    `there is a survivor of the deceased contributor`
    `there is next of kin of the deceased contributor` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `there is an individual or institution who has paid or is responsible for the payment of the deceased contributor's funeral expenses`
           THEN `the individual or institution that paid or is responsible for the payment of the funeral expenses`
        IF `there is a survivor of the deceased contributor` THEN `the survivor of the deceased contributor`
        IF `there is next of kin of the deceased contributor` THEN `the next of kin of the deceased contributor`
        OTHERWISE `nobody under regulation 64`

-- src:642 | (2) No amount in excess of the actual funeral expenses shall be paid pursuant to paragraph (1)(a).
@ref Reg 64(2) (src:642)
GIVEN `the actual funeral expenses` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount of the death benefit` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 64(2) — the most that may be paid to the individual or institution that paid or is responsible for the funeral expenses`
    `the actual funeral expenses` `the amount of the death benefit` MEANS
    min `the actual funeral expenses` `the amount of the death benefit`

-- src:643 | (3) Where, by virtue of subsection (2), an amount paid pursuant to paragraph (1)(a) is less than the amount of the death benefit, a direction pursuant to subsection (1), in so far as it relates to the remainder of the death benefit, may be given as if in the absence of an individual or institution described in that paragraph.
@ref Reg 64(3) (src:643)
GIVEN `the actual funeral expenses` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount of the death benefit` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`reg 64(3) — the remainder of the death benefit that may be directed as if there were no such individual or institution`
    `the actual funeral expenses` `the amount of the death benefit` MEANS
    `the amount of the death benefit`
        MINUS (`reg 64(2) — the most that may be paid to the individual or institution that paid or is responsible for the funeral expenses` `the actual funeral expenses` `the amount of the death benefit`)

@ref Reg 64(3) (src:643)
GIVEN `there is a survivor of the deceased contributor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is next of kin of the deceased contributor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `cr2 Payee of a death benefit other than the estate`
`reg 64(3) — the payee of the remainder` `there is a survivor of the deceased contributor` `there is next of kin of the deceased contributor` MEANS
    `reg 64(1) — the payee of the death benefit when a direction is given` FALSE `there is a survivor of the deceased contributor` `there is next of kin of the deceased contributor`
